# bench/rules/x-sr-plus.lisp and the x-high-when-winning it loads, in full: rules from comparing the Expert with the
# self-play network.  x-sr-combo, plus the non-shooting changes from x-combo: never eclipse, more spade protection, play
# high when winning anyway.

remove rule slead.non.op.void.loser
remove rule sfol.little.over

parameter TriggerHappiness = 999
parameter SpadeProtLen = 5

rule epx.follow.high.when.winning in follow.play weight 65
  reason "EPX - must take it anyway, so play high."
  when
    the lead suit is not spades
    the trick's points are 0
    my legal cards in the lead suit lower than the trick's highest card are empty
  then play the highest of my legal cards

rule sr.lead.low in shoot.lead weight 125
  reason "SR - shooting, leading lowest non-winner."
  then play the lowest of (the non-winners among my legal cards) except my winner suits except the queen
         except the void suits of hearty opponents

rule sr.first.high in shoot.follow weight 110
  reason "SR - shooting, taking the first trick."
  when the trick number is 1
  then play the highest of my legal cards

rule sr.last.take in shoot.follow weight 85
  reason "SR - shooting, taking this one cheaply."
  when
    the trick has 3 cards
    the trick's points are 0
  then play the lowest of my legal cards in the lead suit higher than the trick's highest card

rule sr.little.over in shoot.follow weight 70
  reason "SR - shooting, going a little over, keeping the queen."
  when
    let the cards above be my legal cards in the lead suit higher than the trick's highest card except the queen
    the cards above are not empty
    the number of the cards between the lowest of the cards above and the trick's highest card is at most 4
  then play the lowest of the cards above
